y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+100x–40y+100 & =0 \\\\ (25{x}^{2}+100x)+(4{y}^{2}-40y)+100 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(25{x}^{2}+100x)+(4{y}^{2}-40y)+100 & =0 \\\\ 25[{x}^{2}+4x]+4[{y}^{2}-10y]+100 & =0 \\\\ 25[(x+2)^{2}-{2}^{2}]+4[(y-5)^{2}-{5}^{2}]+100 & =0 \\\\ 25[(x+2)^{2}-4]+4[(y-5)^{2}-25]+100 & =0 \\\\ 25(x+2)^{2}-100+4(y-5)^{2}-100+100 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25(x+2)^{2}-100+4(y-5)^{2}-100+100 & =0 \\\\ 25(x+2)^{2}+4(y-5)^{2} & =-100+100+100 \\\\ 25(x+2)^{2}+4(y-5)^{2} & =100 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $5>2,$ the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot 2=4.$" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329312 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329313 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329314 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329315 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329316 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1041 "selection" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329315 13194139535065 true] [17592186329311 1110 #uuid "ec355938-3070-590c-910b-61d40a6cbe69" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329312 1034 "10" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535065 true] [17592186329312 1111 #uuid "2164137e-eb8f-5f40-9613-df4b68b4f673" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329313 1034 "8" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535065 true] [17592186329313 1111 #uuid "d80af9f1-2cae-5892-a22c-6c69d539acfa" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329314 1034 "2" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1