ter is $(1,-3)$\n- The length of the major axis  is $2\\sqrt{2}$\n- The length of the minor axis is $4$" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329355 1113 #uuid "fd2cdae2-5e26-5778-ab7e-65d79d794e32" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329355 1145 "First, we must group the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x+12y & =-11 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11 \\\\ [{x}^{2}-2x]+2[{y}^{2}+6y] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}]+2[(y+3)^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-1]+2[(y+3)^{2}-9] & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =-11+1+18 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2\\sqrt{2}>2,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2},$ the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the ellipse is centered at $(1,-3).$\n\nTherefore,  I and III are true, and II is false." 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329357 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329358 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329359 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329360 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329361 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1041 "selection" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329358 13194139535065 true] [17592186329356 1110 #uuid "26b3adea-5150-5978-81f3-967d46b5391b" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329357 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535065 true] [17592186329357 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604545